BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:session-1@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261201T092500Z
DTEND:20261201T110000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Session 1: Electrification and the outcomes of COP31 – 
 what scenarios must now capture
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:This opening session examines what accelerated electrification 
 commitments mean for national energy planning. Government planners and the
  institutions supporting them discuss how global electrification goals tra
 nslate into national scenarios\, policies and investment pipelines\, and w
 hat practical support countries need to make that translation work.\n\nPro
 visional programme\, check for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#s
 ession-1
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:session-2@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261201T113000Z
DTEND:20261201T131500Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Session 2: Building planning ecosystems that survive poli
 tical cycles
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Durable scenario work depends on institutions. This session exa
 mines how countries build planning ecosystems that develop and retain capa
 city across ministries\, universities and research institutions\, moving f
 rom dependence on external support toward self-sustaining national plannin
 g functions. It covers institutional mandates and ownership\, skills and r
 etention\, modelling-tool institutionalisation\, and alignment with policy
  and budget cycles.\n\nProvisional programme\, check for changes: https://
 energyplanningweek.info/#session-2
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:session-3@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261124T130616Z
DTSTART:20261201T144500Z
DTEND:20261201T163000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Session 3: Data governance\, sharing and quality assuranc
 e for developing long-term scenarios
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Credible scenarios rest on credible data\, yet many planning te
 ams face fragmented access\, persistent gaps and heavy reliance on proprie
 tary datasets. This session examines how countries and regional institutio
 ns govern\, share and quality-assure energy data – from national energy 
 information systems to regional databases – and explores practical solut
 ions for planning teams with limited resources.\n\nProvisional programme\,
  check for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-3
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-3
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
